{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "SushiSwap",
  "name": "SushiSwap RouteProcessor2 unvalidated route pool",
  "summary": "RouteProcessor2 never checked that the pool encoded in a caller-supplied route was a real UniswapV3 pool. It called swap() on any address and, in uniswapV3SwapCallback, pulled tokenIn with transferFrom from the `from` that the calling 'pool' passed back, so an attacker contract posing as a pool could spend any wallet's RP2 allowance. Exploited on every RP2 deployment.",
