  "notes": [
    "Campaign covers all RP2 deployments found (Ethereum, Arbitrum, Nova, Optimism, BSC, Polygon, Avalanche, Gnosis, Boba). Every drained owner came from Approval logs naming RP2 as spender; each candidate was confirmed by trace. Ethereum's anchor is the earliest drain on any chain.",
    "Excluded as rescues whose proceeds went back to users: Sushi's own SushiFundsReturner bot 0xe0b4ef3a (392 txs, all chains), and 0x869238b1 and 0xcff8bdf5, which each returned their 100 WETH to sifu. c0ffeebabe's 1,000 WETH stays in the loss: it paid 689 ETH to builders and returned only 305 ETH.",
    "Valued at DefiLlama per transaction; bridged stablecoins at par where DefiLlama has no history. 606 pulls of memecoins without a price are valued at zero (rule 15, no realisable market). Later returns, such as the 760 ETH the anchor attacker sent Sushi, are not netted (rule 14)."
